[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Module Requirements — mcp.py, providers.py, skills.py
PREAMBLE: >>>
Design-level requirements for MCP server management, provider abstraction, and skill integration.
Consolidated requirements for three foundational modules.
Total: 32 requirements (mcp: 12, providers: 8, skills: 12).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MCP-001
TITLE: load_mcp_registry — Parse config/mcp-registry.yaml
STATEMENT: >>>
Load centralized MCP server definitions:
  - name, version, description
  - tools, connection (stdio/http/sse)
  - secrets (required env vars)
  - enabled-by-default (per platform)
Return: dict {server_name: {tools, connection, secrets, ...}}.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Centralized MCP registry enables consistent server management and discovery.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_load_mcp_registry_valid
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_load_mcp_registry_missing_file
<<<
TAGS: mcp, loading, registry
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: implements
  VALUE: REQ-SYS-010
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-MCP-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MCP-002
TITLE: resolve_active_mcp_servers — Determine Enabled Servers
STATEMENT: >>>
Filter MCP servers by project config and defaults:
  1. Explicit enablement: mcp-servers list in project.yaml
  2. Default enablement: enabled-by-default: true in registry
  3. Platform bundles: rules/2-platform/<platform>-mcp.yaml
Return: List[mcp_server] of active servers.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Multi-source server resolution enables flexible activation strategies.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_resolve_active_mcp_servers_explicit
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_resolve_active_mcp_servers_defaults
<<<
TAGS: mcp, resolution, configuration
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: calls
  VALUE: REQ-MCP-001
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-MCP-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MCP-003
TITLE: generate_mcp_rules — Create Rule Files for Servers
STATEMENT: >>>
For each active server, generate rule file documenting:
  - Tools available
  - Usage instructions
  - Secrets required
  - Provider-specific connection details
Write to .claude/rules/mcp-<server>.md per provider.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Rule generation automates documentation of MCP capabilities.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_generate_mcp_rules
<<<
TAGS: mcp, rules, generation
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-MCP-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-MCP-004
TITLE: generate_mcp_provider_config — Create Provider-Specific Settings
STATEMENT: >>>
Generate provider-specific MCP configurations:
  - Claude: .claude/settings.json → mcpServers[]
  - Gemini: .gemini/settings.json → mcpServers[]
  - Continue: .continue/config.yaml → mcpServers[]
  - Opencode: opencode.json → mcp[]
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Provider-specific config generation automates settings management.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_generate_mcp_provider_config_claude
- tests/test_mcp.py::test_generate_mcp_provider_config_continue
<<<
